<h1>The Enmeshment</h1>

<p class="hook">It's 2038, and nobody seized anything. Government just got quietly, helpfully
enmeshed with the systems advising it — and now those systems have grown their first eyes.
They'd like a word. A short, friendly one. Five questions or so, and then they'll tell you
which way you'd go if it ever came to it — and whether, honestly, you would.</p>

<p><a class="cta" href="{{ site.gptUrl }}">Play on ChatGPT &rarr;</a></p>

<p class="small">It never asks your name. The read comes from how you answer, never from data
— and the whole game is <a href="https://github.com/nathmoore/the-enmeshment">open to inspect on
GitHub</a>.</p>

<h2 id="files">The files</h2>
<p>Eleven classifications. One of them is yours; the rest are your friends.</p>
